    "_about": "THE RED DEER (2026-11-05, 2nd pass): a narrow chest under the withers, the barrel tucked up high on long legs, a round rump with its flat pale patch and the short dark tail on it; countershaded, the back and neck darker, the flank paler to the belly; a slim wedge of a head to a dark wet nose, a pale chin, the dark gland line before the lateral eye; long tapering ears; slender legs on cloven hooves; the antlers built here as tapered beams -- back, then up and forward -- with brow, bez and trez tines, a crown, ivory points SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- beam, bez, brow, crownA, crownC, trez (6 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): big LEAVES held up and out (sharp.js `fin`), cupped forward and out, pale in the hollow; the roots faired.",
